WEBVTT

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.110
Lisa...

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.600
What do you think?

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.670
It's such a gentle melody.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:08.140
It just melts into my body.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.000
I really like it.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.350
It's a little different from 
usual, but I like this, too.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:14.940
Yeah.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.950
I approve.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.950
I've been meaning to 
share this idea with you.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.140
Why don't you three try 
writing the lyrics this time?

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:30.730
Us?

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:34.980
We've never written lyrics before, though.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:39.800
It sounds fun, but I don't 
know if we can do a good job.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.570
You don't have to overthink it.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:45.850
Just write honestly about what you feel.

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.600
Of course, if you get 
stuck, I can help you out.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.650
Well?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.610
Want to give it a try?

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.770
F-Fine.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:03:01.150
Why don't we show you what we can do, then?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.050
I can't!

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:24.640
I don't know what to write.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.650
Jun, how're you doing?

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.560
Hey, you've got tons.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.850
Don't look!

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.130
Why not?

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.630
We're going to come up with lyrics together.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:37.730
Show me what you've got.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.000
I know, but...

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:44.100
I can't!

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.950
I'm done.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.820
Roll, roll, roll...

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.080
Here.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.380
<b>I love croquettes
I want croquettes
Hot and fluffy croquettes
I want to nom nom</b>

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.380
"I love croquettes.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.750
I want croquettes

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.750
Hot and fluffy croquettes

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.850
I want to nom nom."

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.930
What the heck is this?

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.890
I honestly wrote about what I feel.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:11.640
Well, yeah, you were 
saying that today, but...

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.740
Isn't there anything else?

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.330
Croquettes are my life.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:19.690
Come on...

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.490
Write honestly about what I feel...

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:24.950
Huh...

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.700
The promotional video worked that well, huh?

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.760
Yeah.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.460
I got quite a few inquiries from 
the link I put in the video.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.120
They said they'd come to see any concerts.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.730
That's amazing.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.310
I don't know how many 
people will actually come,

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.880
but I feel like we've taken a step forward.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.350
The rehearsals for the new 
song are coming along, too.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:50.010
Their chemistry is becoming even better, too.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:53.420
I think it might be safe to pick 
a date for the next concert now.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:56.800
Oh, but first, we need 
lyrics for the new song.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.860
Oh, yeah, the girls are 
having a hard time with that.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.700
They don't need to overthink it.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.940
I just need them to put into 
words what they're thinking.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.990
That's pretty hard, though.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.110
Especially for us.

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.840
"Just keep setting foot 
again until you can't.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.590
Even though I fear loss whenever 
every time I meet someone,

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:29.700
I want to live the best I can, 
color life with emotion,

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:33.390
and howl at the beauty of the world."

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.810
That's well-written.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.110
Nukui, you might have talent.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:48.220
I kind of admire people who can do that.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:01.580
<i>Yes?</i>

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.230
It's me, Kyo.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.650
<i>Oh, come in.</i>

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.350
<i>Can you come to the house?</i>

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.370
Thanks for having me.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.620
This is who I was talking 
about earlier, Nukui Kyo-kun.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.870
Have a seat.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:24.610
We have some complicated business.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.840
My name is Alice Stevenson.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:37.130
This is my cousin, Ryan Brunell.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:42.630
Ryan doesn't speak Japanese, 
so he employed an interpreter.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:46.230
You look like you want to say,

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.720
"You're more like a 
marchioness than an Alice."

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.900
No, not at all.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:55.430
Could you please explain 
the situation to Kyo?

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:00.440
I'll get straight to business, 
since I'll be repeating myself.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:04.190
Ryan has a daughter.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.660
Her name is Lisa.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:10.200
One day, she eloped with a Japanese man.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:18.240
The only contact we get from her is the 
photos she takes with her young daughter

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.080
once a year, at Christmas.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:27.150
Ryan was opposed to their marriage 
at first, but he's cooled down now.

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.370
He may not meet them anymore,

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.180
but he's content knowing that 
she's out there living happily.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.340
Or so he thought.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:39.830
But a few years ago, the yearly 
photos stopped coming in.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:43.490
He thought something might 
have happened to her,

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:46.090
so he did everything he 
could to try to find out.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.690
But we still don't know where she is.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.360
He was about to give up, when...

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:54.270
Let me guess, the promotional 
video I uploaded?

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:55.290
Right.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.370
That was a useful lead.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:02.120
And we finally found Lisa's orphaned child.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:07.330
Nozomi's father passed away 
soon after she was born.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:11.680
Her mother had been
raising her all by herself,

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.260
until she was taken by an illness.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:14.620
And so here she is now.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.640
I think I understand the situation.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.890
Let's get to the main 
order of business, then.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:27.650
Ryan would like to adopt Nozomi-san.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:32.900
Of course, Nozomi-san, 
that's only if you desire it.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:41.620
Ryan regrets deeply that he never approved 
your mother and father marrying.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:45.830
So much so that he even feels frustrated 
by his inability to express that himself,

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.170
due to the language barrier.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:52.820
We would like you to come 
live with us in the UK,

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:56.550
where we can provide for all your needs.

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:59.190
It's the least we can do.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:13.760
Master!

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:14.630
Sakura!

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:15.920
Jun! Sora!

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.800
Why aren't you saying anything?

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:20.210
Tell me what you guys think.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:22.700
Tell these people!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.990
Nozomi, sorry,

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:29.510
but you're going to have to think about 
this carefully and decide for yourself.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:33.760
Your future hinges on this. This is important.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:45.810
You all suck!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.090
Zomi!

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.020
Zomi-tan!

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.670
Well, what about you?

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:52.230
Right.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.650
Oh, you sit down.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.430
Zomi!

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.780
Zomi-tan!

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:16.860
There you are.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:32.000
Hey, Kyo, I wonder if anyone 
will think anything if I'm gone.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.650
Of course they would.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.190
Then why...

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:39.860
That's because we want you to be happy.

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.330
I'm happy!

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.120
I'm already happy!

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.140
Yeah.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:49.220
But no one wants to hide that there 
are different ways to find happiness.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:54.440
I think we all want you to compare 
the two and decide for yourself.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:55.370
What?

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:57.310
Who's side are you on, Kyo?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.180
On everyone's.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.970
Including yours.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.050
I'm on everyone's side.

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:22.540
Nozomi remembers her mom, unlike me.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:29.110
I wonder if Zomi-tan is going to the UK.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:37.630
Zomi cried every day when 
she first came here.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.130
She said she misses her mom in heaven.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:47.140
So if she can live with her family...

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:02.200
All right.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:06.820
I'm...

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:10.110
going to go to the UK.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.170
<b>Invitation
</b>Dear Nukui Kyo-sama,
I'm really glad I got to meet you.
Thank you for putting up with our demands.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.980
Tomorrow, huh?

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:31.310
Ryan-san was so happy when 
I said I'd go to the UK.

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.260
So next Sunday,

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:38.690
he's rounding up all his work acquaintances 
in Japan to hold a party to introduce me.

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:41.550
This is your invitation to that.

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:48.430
Onii-chan, are you here?

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:56.500
I heard at school today that 
Nozomi's going to the UK.

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:58.660
Apparently she is.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:01.300
Are you okay with that?

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:03.680
It doesn't matter.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.990
It's what Nozomi decided.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:08.680
But what about Jun and Sora?

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.970
That's for Jun and Sora to decide.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.170
It's not for me to decide.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.190
Kurumi,

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:21.090
want to go the amusement park tomorrow?

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.330
Onii-chan!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.130
Hurry up!

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:06.070
What should we ride next?

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.320
That.

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:15.970
You look stupid.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.830
You're hiding your feelings.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.420
You're even using me to pretend you aren't.

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:27.070
You don't want her to go 
to the UK either, do you?

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:29.050
Well, yeah.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.570
Then why don't you tell her?

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.630
That she can keep living with her friends.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.070
Wouldn't you be happier that way?

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:41.550
It's not how I feel that's important, though.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:47.110
I don't want Nozomi to be 
confused about her own answer.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:50.240
You say that, but you're just afraid.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:54.150
You're just chickening out 
because you don't want to be

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.240
the one to ruin the mood and hurt her.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.370
I'm telling you, you look stupid!

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:15.300
What if Nozomi's the same way?

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:21.120
What if Jun and Sora are too caught up 
worrying about how everyone else is feeling,

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:25.800
and they can't say what they're 
thinking, when somewhere deep inside,

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:31.070
they don't give a damn about the mood 
or about what anyone else is thinking?

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.820
You might be right.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:37.200
But that would be selfish.

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:39.870
Who cares if it's selfish?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:44.340
I'm sure being selfish can 
bring people happiness.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:49.380
I don't know if I can make that happen.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:51.650
I don't know.

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:57.090
But no matter what the outcome is, 
you'll look cool doing it, Onii-chan.

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:15.280
Sorry I'm late.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:23.290
It's okay.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:27.030
Thanks for everything, Kyo.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:28.800
I'm really grateful for your—

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:29.860
Let's not.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.340
Let's not have you go to the UK.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.730
You should live at Little Wing.

00:16:36.730 --> 00:16:39.570
Have fun with the others, 
like you always have.

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:41.850
Let's work on the band together.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.180
Why?

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:49.360
Why are you saying this <i>now</i>?

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.570
I shouldn't have waited.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:57.120
I should have said what I felt a lot sooner.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:01.870
Hey, do you really want 
to go to the UK, Nozomi?

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.700
I made up my mind.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:06.690
So please...

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:09.750
Please, don't say that.

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:17.510
Kyo-san, we thought about it really hard.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:20.860
We decided to send Zomi off 
to the UK with smiles.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:25.070
So let's not give Zomi any more heartache.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.020
I won't.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:32.070
I won't stop until I hear what Nozomi—
what everyone—really thinks.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:36.650
I really want Zomi to be happy.

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:38.150
That's not what I mean.

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.700
It's what <i>you</i> think.

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:44.950
I understand.

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:47.960
I'll say it, then.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.960
I want Zomi...

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:55.470
...not to...

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:58.430
...go to...

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.180
...the UK!

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.650
I want to live with Zomi.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.710
Kyo-san, you idiot.

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:11.870
I tried so hard to hold it in.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:14.250
I held it in every day.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.490
Kyo-nii...

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:27.830
Can I tell Zomi-tan how I really feel, too?

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:33.460
Is it okay if I cry now?

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:34.870
Yeah.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.270
Zomi-tan, don't go.

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:52.980
You have to stay with us forever.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:26.760
<i>Ryan-san was dejected when we 
told him what Nozomi had decided.</i>

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:29.790
<i>But...</i>

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.270
Thank you.

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:36.260
I'm fine.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:46.260
See you again, my grandpa.

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:58.950
Th-Thank you for coming 
to our concert today.

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:04.640
This is the first song 
we've written lyrics for.

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:13.060
At first, we didn't know what to write about.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:18.070
But we've finally figured out how to put 
our own feelings into words honestly.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:23.470
This is how we feel most strongly—
what we want to express.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:26.720
"We Can Hear the Treasure"

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:44.110
<i>Hear the soul</i>

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:56.270
<i>Hear the glimmering</i>

00:20:56.270 --> 00:21:09.950
<i>I wanted to embrace you 
like a warm bowl of soup</i>

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:16.290
<i>It turned out, you felt the same way</i>

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:21.550
<i>I was surprised, but even more, I was happy</i>

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:28.040
<i>You can't help but smile</i>

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:36.100
<i>The treasure I'd been looking 
for was right here all along</i>

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:42.820
<i>My love for you will never die, 
whether you cry or become stubborn</i>

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:56.780
<i>Listen carefully, and you'll 
hear the invisible treasure</i>

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:05.090
Oh, that was wonderful!

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:10.350
What is your band called?

00:22:12.030 --> 00:22:15.340
We need to tell our friends 
when we get back.

00:22:16.260 --> 00:22:20.100
Come to think of, we haven't 
chosen a name for our band yet.

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:21.110
What?

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:25.360
Kyo, think of something.

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:27.460
I can't think of anything on the spot.

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:31.190
These girls don't have a 
name for their band yet.

00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:34.330
Hey.

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:36.950
Let's start the after-party.

00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:39.330
I got a ton of snacks.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:46.460
"Lien de famille."

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:50.800
What does that mean, Saku-chan?

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:52.330
Um...

00:22:52.330 --> 00:22:54.060
"Familial bonds."

00:22:58.150 --> 00:23:00.330
Lien de famille...

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:03.190
Familial bonds.

00:23:03.950 --> 00:23:05.570
The name for our band.

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:08.490
It's decided.

00:23:17.930 --> 00:23:18.810
Yeah!

00:23:21.390 --> 00:23:24.960
<b>Don't Take the Bassist!</b>

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>#07 Surprise Invitation</b>

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:30.410
I took Onii-chan to the amusement park,

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:32.690
and he was thinking about 
something else the whole time.

00:23:32.690 --> 00:23:35.890
<i>He's</i> the one who 
should be repenting, not me!

